#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This means that you can use &kio-locate; by simply typing in konquerors "
"address "
"box. You can e.g. type <command>locate:index.html</command> "
"to find all files that contain \"index.html\" in their name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There's even more: You can use &kio-locate; in all KDE applications that "
"accept "
"URLs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to use this?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use &kio-locate; mostly as you use locate. Instead of typing <command>"
"locate pattern</command> at a command prompt, you start the search with "
"&kio-locate; directly in konqueror. You just enter <command>"
"locate:pattern</command> as the address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, a search <command>locate:pattern</command> "
"is case insensitive if the pattern is lowercase. If the pattern is mixed- or "
"uppercase the search is case sensitive. This default behaviour can be "
"overridden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type <command>locater:config</command> in the konqueror address bar to show "
"the "
"configuration dialog. Likewise, <command>locater:help</command> "
"shows this help document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to write patterns"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Regular wildcard characters may be used in the patterns passed to "
"&kio-locate;: "
"A star (*) matches any string with nonzero length, a question mark (?) "
"matches "
"a single character, and a character list ([abc-z]) matches the characters in "
"the list. A character list can be inverted by putting a caret after the first "
"square bracket ([^abc-z])."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every plus (+) in a search is used just as a star (*) is. Instead of <command>"
"locate:*.html</command> you may also type <command> locate:+.html</command>"
". This is because you can't use the star in konqueror. In other apps both "
"ways "
"are supported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Should you need to use a plus in your search you have to escape it with a "
"backslash. Instead of <command>locate:g++</command> you have to use <command>"
"locate:g\\+\\+</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore you can't use a slash as the last character of your query. O.k. "
"you "
"can, but KDE will ignore it. In such a case you can quote your pattern: Write "
"<command>locate:\"servicemenus/\"</command> rather than <command>"
"locate:servicemenus/</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A search as e.g. <command>locate:~/*.doc</command> works as you might expect. "
"This means that <command>~/</command> and <command> ~user/</command> "
"are expanded correctly at the beginning of the pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may add a filtering pattern after the first pattern, e.g. <command>"
"locate:fish home</command> results in all files whose path contains fish AND "
"home."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A filtering pattern may be inverted by prefixing it with an exclamation mark. "
"E.g. <command>locate:fish !home</command> results in all files whose path "
"contains fish AND NOT home."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "Any number of filtering patterns may be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <command>locate:</command> wildcard matching is performed with all "
"patterns. If you're a regular expression guru, you might want to use <command>"
"rlocate:</command>, which enables regexp matching for all filtering patterns "
"(that is: all patterns except the first one)."
msgstr ""

